			<div class="forum_comment_action_menu" style="display: none;" id="forum_comment_actions_menu_562546398187387886">				<a class="forum_comment_action report tooltip" href="javascript:Forum_ShowReportDialog( '103582791474736036', '4847652375936776257', '562546398187387886', '38719117', '-1' );" data-tooltip-text="Report this post for inappropriate content.  Reported post are flagged for review by moderators.">
				<span class="non_breaking_space">&nbsp;</span><img src="https://community.fastly.steamstatic.com/public/images/skin_1/notification_icon_flag_dark.png?v=1">Report this post</a>
			</div>
						
		</div>

		<div class="topic" id="forum_op_topic_562546398187387886">
		So how does the AI stuff work, exactly? And how much content is in the game?	</div>
	<div class="content" id="forum_op_content_562546398187387886">
		The concept sounds VERY cool and I'm interested, but I'm also cautious since its early access (many EA games fall over or get rushed out the door just to be done with it) and AI heavy (many AI games fall over or get rushed out the door because working with AI is expensive).<br><br>So, you know, AI EA game sounds like double the risk yanno? So I wanna know if this game is &quot;future proofed&quot; if it gets abandoned or whatever.<br><br>Firstly, I want to make sure I understand how the AI works. I get that you get a starting amount of crystals and its enough to make 3 or 4 characters, and you can have 10 AI generated responses per in-game day? If you want more, go buy more crystals? Or are you expected to buy that starting pack DLC for that?<br><br>I believe that once a character is made, they can operate as a normal NPC without AI involvement? So if the AI part falls over, at least you still have the game? You only need AI and crystals for the initial generation of a character and if you want live responses? I see the store page mentions AI generated backstories, quests and items though but does that come out of your pocket? Like, if an NPC decides to bombard you with 5 fetch quests at once is that your fault?<br><br>Also, the fact that items are AI generated makes me wonder if there's ways to abuse the process. Like you make a character who is very rich and generous and gives away powerful items, and then you bug them to give you powerful items.<br><br>Anyway, my main concern is about how much it costs to run the AI parts of the game and what happens if the AI part fails/shuts down/gets abandoned. Like, what actually happens? What still functions and what breaks?<br><br>Secondly, how much content is in the game right now? Like, if I bought it and the game never updated again would I feel like I got my money's worth? EA games man, you never know, yanno?<br><br>Thanks and cheers.	</div>
		
	<div class="forum_op_footer">
		<div></div>
			</div>
</div>
<div data-featuretarget="community-awards"></div>
<script type="text/javascript">
	$J( function() {
		InitializeForumTopic( {"owner":"45214628","type":"General","feature":"0","gidforum":"4847652375936776257","forum_display_name":"General Discussions","forum_url":"https:\/\/steamcommunity.com\/app\/2990190\/discussions\/0\/","forum_search_url":"https:\/\/steamcommunity.com\/app\/2990190\/discussions\/search\/","is_public":1,"permissions":{"can_view":1,"can_post":1,"can_reply":1,"is_banned":0,"can_delete":0,"can_edit":0},"appid":2990190}, "https:\/\/steamcommunity.com\/forum\/45214628\/General\/",
		"562546398187387886", {"author":"Kyubox","text":"The concept sounds VERY cool and I'm interested, but I'm also cautious since its early access (many EA games fall over or get rushed out the door just to be done with it) and AI heavy (many AI games fall over or get rushed out the door because working with AI is expensive).\n\nSo, you know, AI EA game sounds like double the risk yanno? So I wanna know if this game is \"future proofed\" if it gets abandoned or whatever.\n\nFirstly, I want to make sure I understand how the AI works. I get that you get a starting amount of crystals and its enough to make 3 or 4 characters, and you can have 10 AI generated responses per in-game day? If you want more, go buy more crystals? Or are you expected to buy that starting pack DLC for that?\n\nI believe that once a character is made, they can operate as a normal NPC without AI involvement? So if the AI part falls over, at least you still have the game? You only need AI and crystals for the initial generation of a character and if you want live responses? I see the store page mentions AI generated backstories, quests and items though but does that come out of your pocket? Like, if an NPC decides to bombard you with 5 fetch quests at once is that your fault?\n\nAlso, the fact that items are AI generated makes me wonder if there's ways to abuse the process. Like you make a character who is very rich and generous and gives away powerful items, and then you bug them to give you powerful items.\n\nAnyway, my main concern is about how much it costs to run the AI parts of the game and what happens if the AI part fails\/shuts down\/gets abandoned. Like, what actually happens? What still functions and what breaks?\n\nSecondly, how much content is in the game right now? Like, if I bought it and the game never updated again would I feel like I got my money's worth? EA games man, you never know, yanno?\n\nThanks and cheers."}		);
			} );
</script>
										<script type="text/javascript">
$J( function() { InitializeCommentThread( "ForumTopic", "ForumTopic_103582791474736036_4847652375936776257_562546398187387886", {"feature":"4847652375936776257","feature2":"562546398187387886","owner":"103582791474736036","commentthreadid":"662414465","total_count":4,"start":0,"pagesize":15,"has_upvoted":0,"upvotes":0,"votecountid":null,"voteupid":null,"commentcountid":null,"subscribed":false,"extended_data":"{\"topic_permissions\":{\"can_view\":1,\"can_post\":1,\"can_reply\":1,\"is_banned\":0,\"can_delete\":0,\"can_edit\":0},\"original_poster\":38719117,\"topic_gidanswer\":\"0\",\"forum_appid\":2990190,\"forum_public\":1,\"forum_type\":\"General\",\"forum_gidfeature\":\"0\"}","oldestfirst":true,"comments_raw":{"562546398187390253":{"text":"Oh yeah, now that I think about it, how is content moderation with AI? Like, am I gonna get hit with \"as an AI model i cannot-\" type stuff if i ask for something that's too bloody, gory or sexy?","author":"Kyubox"},"562546398187460384":{"text":"Just so you aren't left hanging, I'll try tossing my two cents in here: Any video game that incorporates live AI services is going to disappear someday. Everything about AI is a giant money sinkhole, and the general business model is to nickel and dime users with premium currency purchases.\nYou know what you are comfortable spending, and I don't really care to tell you what you should or shouldn't do with your money. But to answer your question about future proofing, I don't think that's something that any AI-centric developer would want to entertain overly much. The developer is constantly burning money for as long as the game remains up, so from a business perspective, this game needs to make a lot of cash as fast as possible and they can't have people opt out of paying for anything if they can help it.\n\nThe developer is playing chicken with the consumer, watching their bank account rise and fall month by month, trying to determine when the best moment to pull out and secure their winnings will be. If people are using the AI without finding any excuse to throw money at the developer for more premium currency, then it actually ends up losing them money just to leave it up. In the best case scenario, enough whales get hooked that they keep feeding the developer fistfuls of cash month after month, paying enough for all the freemium users to coast by, cushioning whatever financial blow they're producing for the dev.\n\nAI microtransactions aren't all that different from loot boxes, you roll the dice, maybe you get something that gives you a small dopamine spike if you get a good roll, and then you go back to grinding. Instead of gun skins or digital cards, you get a paragraph of text that miiiiight make sense and miiiight be pleasant to read, and will probably look very similar to the other eight paragraphs of text you've been given up that point since AI has a habit of homogenizing everything.\nI guess what I'm saying is that what you're paying for here is even more ephemeral than what you get out of a gacha or loot box, so concerns about \"future proofing\" might be missing the forest through the trees.\n\nIf it's the gameplay you're after, I personally feel like you'd probably get more out of games like Elin or Creator of Another World, because I'm fairly confident in saying that you won't find satisfaction in what the AI chat bot replies to you with and if you strip the game of that gimmick, it looks like a lesser version of already existing games. (And again, that gimmick of live AI interactions is predicated on constant premium currency purchases to keep the developer from pulling out with whatever earnings they've secured before the AI services drain their wallet dry, so it's best to evaluate the game itself rather than the temporary gimmick it's trying to sell folks on.)","author":"Whispierre"},"562546398187461098":{"text":"The developer of the game has released a beta function to allow people to use their own models. Image generation still uses the official model but the devs are looking into allowing people to use their own models for that as well.","author":"Kiryuu Sonya"},"562546398187465262":{"text":"[quote=Whispierre;562546398187460384]\n\nIf it's the gameplay you're after, I personally feel like you'd probably get more out of games like Elin or Creator of Another World [\/quote]\n\nOh. I thought this was a farming based game like stardew valley based on all the farming screenshots. I hate games like Elin, Elona and Dwarf Fortress. If this game is like that, I don't care anymore.","author":"Kyubox"}},"track_navigation":true}, 'https://steamcommunity.com/comment/ForumTopic/', 40 ); } );
</script>
